<title>INDIA: Indian castor trade closed in tax hike strike.</title>
<headline>Indian castor trade closed in tax hike strike.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian castor markets were closed on Thursday in a strike called by traders to oppose increased taxes, dealers said. Trading will resume on Friday.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, Indian castorseed March delivery prices fell to 1,167/1,168 rupees per quintal from 1,174/1,175 rupees in the absence of fresh export demand, dealers said.</p>
<p>Traders are protesting the increase in sales tax and other charges from January 1 by the government in western Maharashtra state, where Bombay is located.</p>
<p>-- Bombay Commodities +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
